course: dictionary
lesson: 15940
title: Formal words: unserviceable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unserviceable means broken or worn out, so it is no longer fit to use. Look inside the word: un- means not, and serviceable means fit to use. Put them together and you get not fit to use. «The lift is unserviceable.» The clue is in the parts, so you can work it out.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «The swings are unserviceable, so the school has put up a sign.» A school puts up a sign when something is dangerous or cannot be used. Swap in your meaning: «The swings are broken, so the school has put up a sign.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: You will mostly meet this word in formal writing, such as reports, letters from councils, army notes and airline announcements. «The playground equipment is unserviceable.» In everyday talk, people would say broken, useless or out of order. Knowing both kinds of words helps you read official notices and talk to friends.
fact: Unserviceable means broken or worn out and no longer fit to use.
fact: The word un- means not, so unserviceable means not fit to use.
fact: «The old tyre is unserviceable.» This means the tyre is worn out and cannot be used.
fact: Unserviceable is a formal word, found in reports, letters and official notices.
fact: Everyday words with a similar meaning are broken, useless and out of order.
exercise: «The lift is unserviceable, so please use the stairs.» What does unserviceable mean? | Very tall and shiny | *Broken and not fit to use | Full of people | Newly painted
exercise: Which everyday word means the same as unserviceable? | *Out of order | Ancient | Bright | Hungry
exercise: The airline said the seat belt was unserviceable. What does this suggest? | It was the best seat on the plane | *It could not be used safely | It was very loud | It was brand new
test: «The council closed the park because the gate was unserviceable.» Why was the park closed? | Because the park was too full of people | Because the gate was brand new | Because it was raining and the grass was wet | *Because the gate was broken and could not be used
test: Which word could replace unserviceable in «The machine is unserviceable»? | Loud | *Broken | Hungry | Brand new
exam: «The report said the fire engine was unserviceable.» What does the report mean? | The engine was too big for the road | The engine was full of water | The engine had just been washed and painted red | *The engine was broken and could not be used
